WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.758
Restaurant and Café.

2
00:00:02.038 --> 00:00:06.347
Day 33 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:08.097 --> 00:00:09.121
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.401 --> 00:00:13.881
Ordering food is a good confidence workout: short, friendly and low-risk.

5
00:00:14.161 --> 00:00:17.361
Team dinners and client lunches use the same phrases.

6
00:00:18.711 --> 00:00:19.565
Part 1.

7
00:00:19.845 --> 00:00:20.719
Arriving.

8
00:00:21.969 --> 00:00:23.548
A table for two, please.

9
00:00:23.828 --> 00:00:26.623
We have a reservation under Gupta, 8 pm.

10
00:00:26.903 --> 00:00:30.188
Could we sit by the window or outside or somewhere quieter?

11
00:00:30.468 --> 00:00:31.769
How long is the wait?

12
00:00:33.119 --> 00:00:33.994
Part 2.

13
00:00:34.274 --> 00:00:35.063
Ordering.

14
00:00:36.313 --> 00:00:37.657
Here is a quick table:

15
00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.324
Situation, and Say.

16
00:00:39.604 --> 00:00:40.521
Need time:

17
00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:42.551
Could we have a few more minutes, please?

18
00:00:42.831 --> 00:00:44.367
Ask for a recommendation:

19
00:00:44.647 --> 00:00:45.820
What do you recommend?

20
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.295
What's popular here?

21
00:00:47.575 --> 00:00:48.769
Dietary needs:

22
00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:52.377
I'm vegetarian or vegan or allergic to peanuts.

23
00:00:52.657 --> 00:00:54.215
Does this dish contain any?

24
00:00:54.495 --> 00:00:55.455
Customise:

25
00:00:55.735 --> 00:00:59.532
Could I have this less spicy or without onions or sauce on the side?

26
00:00:59.812 --> 00:01:00.601
Ordering:

27
00:01:00.881 --> 00:01:03.975
I'll have the paneer tikka, and could I get a lime soda?

28
00:01:04.255 --> 00:01:05.044
Portion:

29
00:01:05.324 --> 00:01:07.820
Is this enough for two, or should we order more?

30
00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:08.889
Coffee:

31
00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:11.665
A medium cappuccino with oat milk, please.

32
00:01:11.945 --> 00:01:13.247
For here or to go.

33
00:01:14.597 --> 00:01:15.493
Part 3.

34
00:01:15.773 --> 00:01:16.754
During the meal.

35
00:01:18.004 --> 00:01:20.607
Excuse me, could we get some more water, please?

36
00:01:20.887 --> 00:01:22.764
Sorry, this isn't what I ordered.

37
00:01:23.044 --> 00:01:24.601
I asked for the grilled fish.

38
00:01:24.881 --> 00:01:26.375
The food is a bit cold.

39
00:01:26.655 --> 00:01:28.041
Could you warm it up, please?

40
00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:30.199
Everything was delicious, thank you!

41
00:01:31.549 --> 00:01:32.466
Part 4.

42
00:01:32.746 --> 00:01:33.557
The bill.

43
00:01:34.807 --> 00:01:36.727
Could we have the bill or the check, please?

44
00:01:37.007 --> 00:01:39.460
Can we split the bill? / I'll get this one.

45
00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:41.681
Do you accept cards or UPI?

46
00:01:41.961 --> 00:01:43.583
Is service charge included?

47
00:01:44.933 --> 00:01:45.573
Tip:

48
00:01:45.853 --> 00:01:47.709
Hosting a client or team dinner.

49
00:01:47.989 --> 00:01:49.397
Let guests order first.

50
00:01:49.677 --> 00:01:51.981
Suggest 2 to 3 dishes if they're unsure.

51
00:01:52.261 --> 00:01:54.821
Avoid heavy work talk until the food arrives.

52
00:01:55.101 --> 00:01:59.175
Settle the bill quietly (tell the waiter in advance, or step away to pay).

53
00:02:00.525 --> 00:02:01.485
Part 5.

54
00:02:01.765 --> 00:02:03.195
Practice conversations.

55
00:02:04.445 --> 00:02:06.151
Ordering with dietary needs.

56
00:02:06.431 --> 00:02:08.458
Here is how the conversation goes.

57
00:02:08.738 --> 00:02:09.741
Good evening.

58
00:02:10.021 --> 00:02:11.514
Are you ready to order?

59
00:02:11.794 --> 00:02:12.775
Almost.

60
00:02:13.055 --> 00:02:15.722
Could you tell me what's in the chef's special curry?

61
00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.986
It has paneer, cashews and cream.

62
00:02:18.266 --> 00:02:20.399
My friend is allergic to nuts.

63
00:02:20.679 --> 00:02:22.749
Can it be made without cashews?

64
00:02:23.029 --> 00:02:24.437
Yes, we can do that.

65
00:02:25.787 --> 00:02:27.387
The conversation continues.

66
00:02:27.667 --> 00:02:28.413
Great.

67
00:02:28.693 --> 00:02:33.728
We'll have one chef's special without cashews, one dal tadka, and four rotis.

68
00:02:34.008 --> 00:02:35.352
Anything to drink?

69
00:02:35.632 --> 00:02:37.424
Two sweet lassis, please.

70
00:02:37.704 --> 00:02:39.389
And could we have some water?

71
00:02:39.669 --> 00:02:40.373
Sure.

72
00:02:40.653 --> 00:02:41.784
Anything else?

73
00:02:42.064 --> 00:02:43.856
That's all for now, thank you.

74
00:02:45.206 --> 00:02:46.593
Wrong order and the bill.

75
00:02:46.873 --> 00:02:48.899
Here is how the conversation goes.

76
00:02:49.179 --> 00:02:52.294
Excuse me, I think this isn't what we ordered.

77
00:02:52.574 --> 00:02:55.710
We asked for dal tadka, not dal makhani.

78
00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:57.227
I'm so sorry.

79
00:02:57.507 --> 00:02:59.086
I'll change it right away.

80
00:02:59.366 --> 00:03:00.305
Thank you.

81
00:03:00.585 --> 00:03:01.395
Later

82
00:03:01.675 --> 00:03:03.275
Could we have the bill, please?

83
00:03:04.625 --> 00:03:06.225
The conversation continues.

84
00:03:06.505 --> 00:03:07.529
Here you are.

85
00:03:07.809 --> 00:03:11.244
I think we've been charged for the dal makhani as well.

86
00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.231
You're right, I apologise.

87
00:03:13.511 --> 00:03:14.705
I'll correct it.

88
00:03:14.985 --> 00:03:16.180
No problem.

89
00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.359
Can we pay by UPI?

90
00:03:18.639 --> 00:03:20.836
And is the service charge included?

91
00:03:21.116 --> 00:03:24.551
Yes, UPI is fine, and the service charge is included.

92
00:03:25.901 --> 00:03:27.501
The conversation continues.

93
00:03:27.781 --> 00:03:28.719
Thank you.

94
00:03:28.999 --> 00:03:30.599
The food was delicious.

95
00:03:31.949 --> 00:03:33.485
That's the end of this lesson.

96
00:03:33.765 --> 00:03:38.416
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

97
00:03:38.696 --> 00:03:44.819
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

